  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban Internet Connectivity Expansion, through Baylis Digital</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant to Poa Internet Kenya Limited, a Kenya-based internet service provider, supports the expansion of affordable fixed wireless internet access to an additional 1 million households in low-income urban communities across Africa. The Study is assessing the market opportunity in Algeria, Cameroon, Cte d&apos;Ivoire, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Ghana, Morocco, Mozambique, Nigeria, Senegal, Sierra Leone, South Africa, Tanzania, Uganda, and Zambia, and thereafter recommending three target markets for Poa&apos;s expansion.</narrative>
  </description>
